---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Installation">
  <div>
    <a href="/docs" class="back-link">← Back to documentation</a>

    <h1>Installation</h1>
    <p>Desktop-2FA is a Python package for Windows, macOS, and Linux. Python 3.11 or newer is required.</p>

    <h2>Install with pip</h2>
    <pre><code>python -m pip install desktop-2fa</code></pre>

    <h2>Install with pipx</h2>
    <p>pipx installs the command-line application in an isolated environment:</p>
    <pre><code>pipx install desktop-2fa</code></pre>

    <h2>Upgrade</h2>
    <p>The current release is 0.10.0 (October 30, 2026). Create an encrypted backup before upgrading and review <a href="/docs/vault">compatibility notes</a>, especially password-file whitespace handling.</p>
    <pre><code>d2fa backup
python -m pip install --upgrade desktop-2fa</code></pre>
    <p>For pipx installations, use <code>pipx upgrade desktop-2fa</code>.</p>
    <h2>Verify and get started</h2>
    <pre><code>d2fa --version
d2fa --help
d2fa vault init</code></pre>

    <p>To install from source:</p>
    <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/wrogistefan/desktop-2fa
cd desktop-2fa
python -m pip install .</code></pre>

    <p>See the <a href="/docs/cli">CLI reference</a> for commands and the{' '}<a href="/docs/vault">vault guide</a> for backup and path options.</p>
    <p><a href="https://pypi.org/project/desktop-2fa/">PyPI project page</a> ·
      <a href="https://github.com/wrogistefan/desktop-2fa/releases">GitHub releases</a></p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
